A||||15||batboy||Batmobile at triple digits||||11||
Z||000000||batboy||07-23-2000||03:45 PM||||Well I was out today goofing around in my V8 Fiero. Did a couple 0-60 mph blasts...still can't get under 6 seconds. Then I got a wild hair up my butt and ran the Batmobile up to 100 mph...see pic below...kids, don't try this at home.<P>A few minutes later, I hopped onto the 4 lane highway and soon I was getting cut off by a big redneck in a big pickup pulling a big livestock trailer. I layed on the horn and ended up driving on the shoulder, almost in the ditch at 70 mph, to avoid getting rubbed out.<P>This guy follows me off the Interstate and at the exit ramp stop sign, I got out to discuss my displeasure at getting run off the road. I was still angry because he about creamed me, so I wasn't being too polite. Ok, I might of said, "Hey ******* , if you don't know how to drive that rig, than get off the highway before you kill someone!" Well, he told me he was sorry and didn't see me in his blind spot, but then started pointing and shaking his finger in my face while telling me I'd better cool down because he was bigger than me.<P>He continued lecturing me like I was a child until I told him to get that finger out of my face before I break it off. He took a step back and looked surprised. I told him that he was bigger than me, but I wasn't afraid of one old fat man and to get his sorry butt back into his truck before I really got mad. He let out a big sigh and got back into his truck. Whew, sometimes bluffing works.<P>A few minutes later, I noticed a huge blue cloud of smoke rolling out from behind the car and up out of the rear deck louvers. Oh guano, now what?!? I had a major oil leak somewhere and engine oil had gotten sprayed everywhere. It was running down all over the exhaust manifolds and mufflers which was cooking it causing all the smoke. The fire hazard was extremely high at this point.<P>I let everything cool off and added a quart of oil (I always carry an extra bottle of oil). I had no tools and was still half a quart low, so I limped back home at a sedate pace, stopped occasionally to cool the car down and to check everything over. I used another 1/2 quart in the 20 miles it took to get home. I guess that's my punishment for cussing out a stupid redneck who can't drive. Or maybe I'm being punished for taking a photo while driving triple digits...I don't know. Probably a seal was ready to let go and my screwing around in the Batmobile popped a leak. I hate this...everyone of my cars has something needing fixed right now. Boohoo!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bat100mph.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||07-23-2000||04:16 PM||||Where are the mountains? I don't see any mountains! <P>Know how you feel bat. I almost got squished by an 18 wheeler on a very rainy day on the freeway. His tires were kicking up so much spray that he couldn't see me (and I didn't have my lights on). I slammed it into 3rd and hit the shoulder. As I got around him he flashed his lights at me. I think that ment he was sorry?<P>Figure out what's wrong hit the batmobile yet?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||07-23-2000||04:52 PM||||You didn't mess up your oil pan while off-roading did you?<P>Good luck||||reg||5
Z||000003||snowkttn||07-23-2000||05:51 PM||||Wow....what a ride batboy......sorry to hear about the trouble with your car.  I would have loved to have been in the passenger seat when you stomped on it though *grin*<BR>(snowkttn loves speed)||||reg||6
Z||000004||fsrowsell||07-23-2000||06:20 PM||||Batboy, what gauges do you have in your car?||||reg||1
