Z||000006||batboy||07-23-2000||08:52 PM||||Ok kids, been out crawling over and under the Batmobile. There is a fresh dent in the oil pan, but that's not where it's leaking. The oil pan gasket on the back side (right side in a regular car) is leaking. Most of the pan bolts were super loose. I'm guessing whatever smacked the bottom of the oil pan jarred the gasket loose since the bolts weren't tight. The leaking oil ran down onto the exhaust pipes and started smoking, which probably saved me from running the Batmobile out of oil. I snugged up the bolts, gotta be carefully tightening up an old gasket, sometimes that makes the leak worse. Anyway, it appears to have slowed the leak down considerably. It's still oozing a tiny bit, but at least it's not spraying oil everywhere like it was. I'll have to eventually pull the pan off and replace the gasket...not a fun job if it's even possible.<P>Sorry if it sounded like I was being a hothead, but that was a scary white knuckle ride that could of been a very bad scene. Guano happens very fast at 70 mph on the highway. If that guy would of just said "soory guy, didn't see you" and then let it drop, it would of been cool. But, for him to get in my face and shake that finger at me like I was a bad little batboy, well...it really made me mad.<P>SCCA, mountains in Kansas? We have hills, but no mountains. But, you knew that.<P>Pontiaddict, I think maybe you're right. Too bad I didn't see your post until after I found out what the problem was.<P>Snowkttn, the next time I'm in your neighborhood, I'll give you a "quick" ride in the Batmobile if you'll give me a ride in your little Snowmobile.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Also, I've been trying to post a pic of your GT on my site, but I can't upload any files right now.<P>Fsrowsell, the speedo and tach are Auto Meter Sport Comp series gauges. They look good in the car I think. However, they were not that easy to install, although they look like they fit right in don't they. I spent the better part of one whole weekend trimming, cutting, grinding, filing, trial fitting, etc. before I was happy with the way they fit. I even had to modify the mounting brackets. One of the gauges had an illumination bulb socket that stuck out too far in the back. I contacted Auto Meter about it and they sent me a special flush mounting bulb socket that didn't stick out the back...free of charge. Now that's customer service.||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||07-23-2000||09:04 PM||||No photo radar in my county, I don't think the State police even have it here in Kansas that I know of. Maybe in Kansas City or Wichita. Anyway, that 100 mph blast was on an open blacktop county road with no traffic that I could see for about 2 miles either direction. Plus, I knew where the deputy sheriff was that patrols the area.<P>Look at the tach...it's just loafing at 4200 rpm. The car was still pulling strong at the century mark. I'm sure I can peg the speedo (if I wanted too) once I get new tires (and the oil leak fixed).||||reg||1
Z||000008||86SE||07-24-2000||03:10 AM||||Whats that Fiero's redline?  And what kind of trans is in it?<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Fiero||||reg||14
Z||000009||batboy||07-24-2000||07:22 AM||||I have an auto tranny and have been using a 5,000 rpm shift redline, but a small block Chevy with a stock valvetrain (like mine) will probably do 5,500 rpm with no problem, and maybe even a very quick blast to 6,000 rpm, but that's getting borderline with valve float with old high mileage valve springs. I still had my foot into it when I snapped the pic. When I let up a little to cruise, of course with having an auto, the rpm settles back down several rpm lower, especially when the torque converter locks up.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Richard Parnell||07-24-2000||02:20 PM||||Careful posting that pic of your car doing 100.  I was watching some dumb show on tv where they have a film of a guy doing 150-170 on a freeway, the picture had an insert of his speedo.  He was selling the video on the net and got busted for speeding via the tape, strange huh?||||reg||12
